From 4cd1e4340180fd8a3474773c7f800ef2506e1aff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:01:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] soc: qcom: icc-bwmon: don't log the expected
 busy-region claim

On MSM8998 both BWMON regions sit inside the BIMC window the interconnect
driver already owns, so the claim fails by design and bwmon_ioremap()
falls back to a plain mapping. It still went through
devm_platform_ioremap_resource() first, which reports each failure at
error level, so every probe logged two "can't request region" errors for
a device that was working fine.

Claim the region directly and quietly, ignore the result, and map it
either way. SoCs whose regions are free keep the claim.

Prior art and credits: refines "soc: qcom: icc-bwmon: share the BWMON
regions with the BIMC driver" (f93453cc79e0), from the scada joan tree.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
index 1848f4a41..b7522c669 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
@@ -729,16 +729,18 @@ static irqreturn_t bwmon_intr_thread(int irq, void *dev_id)
  */
 static void __iomem *bwmon_ioremap(struct platform_device *pdev, unsigned int index)
 {
-	void __iomem *base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, index);
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct resource *res;
-
-	if (PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(base) != -EBUSY)
-		return base;
+	void __iomem *base;
 
 	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, index);
 	if (!res)
 		return IOMEM_ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
-	base = devm_ioremap(&pdev->dev, res->start, resource_size(res));
+
+	/* A busy region is the expected case here, not an error to report. */
+	devm_request_mem_region(dev, res->start, resource_size(res), dev_name(dev));
+
+	base = devm_ioremap(dev, res->start, resource_size(res));
 	return base ?: IOMEM_ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 }
 
